##
An index past the end of a set.

This program compiles. How many values a set holds is not known until it runs, so an
index that is too large is caught at the moment it is used.
##

global model Program
    function Main()
        integer[] scores = {90, 72, 88};

        # One past the last, which is the classic off-by-one: the last index is 2.
        for i = 0 to scores.Count()
            Console.WriteLine(scores[i]);
        end for
    end function
end model
